WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.867
Former President Trump's

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.801
new federal indictment

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.870
isn't just another legal battle.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.372
It's not just another political battle.

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:07.340
It's unprecedented in every way.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.241
The current frontrunner

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.042
for the GOP

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.611
nomination is the first former president

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.947
in U.S. history to face federal charges.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:15.682
This is the second indictment

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.550
for the former president just months ago.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.085
He became the first ex-president

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.021
to be charged with a criminal offense,

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.089
getting charged in New York with 34

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:23.857
felony counts

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:24.924
relating to the Stormy

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.960
Daniels hush money payments.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.595
Well, joining us to somehow,

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:29.729
someway put this into

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.064
perspective is Tim Naftali,

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:31.965
CNN presidential

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.666
historian, former director

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.935
of the Nixon Presidential Library.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.704
In a time there's

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:38.738
some common wording

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:41.074
when you read the reporting

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:41.975
this morning, New York

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.309
Times, Washington Post,

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:43.810
The Times

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:44.511
writing the Justice

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:45.512
Department on Thursday

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.312
took the legally

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:47.781
and politically momentous step.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:48.281
The Post

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:48.648
calling it

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.350
a, quote, seismic event

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.384
in the nation's political

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:52.619
and legal history.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:55.388
Is presidential in the middle of legal

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.956
and political history?

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.092
Venn diagram?

00:00:59.092 --> 00:00:59.692
Well,

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.027
why don't we step back

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.562
and look at what's at issue

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.764
and then maybe people do.

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.332
Easier for people to understand why

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.767
this is a seismic moment.

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:11.771
I don't think many Americans

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:13.106
would be that concerned

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:14.140
if the president,

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.141
in leaving the White House,

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.644
took things that he shouldn't have taken

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.246
because it's a hurly burly,

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.848
big rush at the end,

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:24.184
especially when you have a transition

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.251
that that president didn't

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.219
believe should happen.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:26.586
All right.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.620
2021 was,

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.188
as we know,

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:30.457
a dramatic year, to put it mildly,

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.661
But it's the issue of keeping

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:35.762
the material.

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:36.763
When the US government

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:37.330
said, Hey,

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.732
you've got stuff that you shouldn't.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.434
And then when that stuff includes

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:44.471
Topsy, acrid materials

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.106
and it appears that the president,

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:48.475
former president shared them with people

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:52.579
and then it appears directed others

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:55.181
to move them so that Federal

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.050
National Archives

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.918
employees and federal lawyers

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.019
couldn't get at them.

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.388
Then it opens up the question of

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.924
is someone above the law

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.826
because they became president?

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:07.927
That's the question

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:08.728
I think people should

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:09.896
keep in their minds.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:12.198
Do you want to live in a country

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.300
or once someone is elected president,

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.636
they can decide which laws to follow

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.171
and which laws not to follow?

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:18.438
I mean,

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:20.640
I think that's the basic issue here.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.575
And it's beyond

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.110
the time of the presidency,

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.412
which I think is important to focus on.

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:27.814
These charges are about

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:28.515
what happened

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:29.749
after he left office

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:30.783
and the consistent claim

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.252
from the former president,

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.853
despite his shifting defense

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.522
about how he says he declassified it

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:37.590
with his mind or whatever,

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.125
is that he believes

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.095
that because he was president,

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:44.030
he has this right,

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:44.597
his right

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:47.033
to have all of these things, Poppy.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.536
I think this is a symptom

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:52.105
of a problem with the entire Trump

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.940
presidency, where President Trump

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.242
understood that he got powers

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:56.943
when he was elected,

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.044
but he didn't understand

00:02:58.044 --> 00:02:59.746
that he had obligations

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.114
and that we live in a constant

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:03.249
to tional democracy.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.484
Everybody,

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:06.186
including the president, is bound

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:06.986
by that constitution

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.788
and there are limits to their power.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.456
And President Trump

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.625
not only had a hard time with limits,

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.060
he didn't respect them.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:14.961
And this is a case

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:17.430
where he was told repeatedly

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.999
that there were limits to his ability

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.901
to keep materials and he said,

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:22.702
I don't care.

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:23.670
We're going to hear a lot,

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:24.804
I think, from the Trump

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.139
defense team, from Trump

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:26.673
allies

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.208
about the Presidential Records Act.

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:29.509
The president has brought that up a lot.

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:31.711
And just to be very, very clear,

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.079
the the former director

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:34.581
of the National Archives has said

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:35.882
very clearly that that is just

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.550
they are wrong as a matter of law

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.585
to say that it extends

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:39.586
beyond the minutes

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:41.020
that he's not president

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.455
saying when President Biden took office,

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:43.890
all presidential records of the Trump

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:44.624
administration came

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:45.792
into the legal custody

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:47.327
of the archives of the United States.

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:49.028
There's no legal question about that.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.029
In fact,

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:50.897
not none whatsoever

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:53.132
I mean, I was a federal library director.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.001
My particular president

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:56.169
was Richard Nixon,

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:58.071
who actually gave birth to all of this

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:00.673
because he wanted to destroy records that

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:02.609
would have put him in legal peril.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:04.377
Let me

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.445
let's make it absolutely clear

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:06.479
to everybody.

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:08.615
You, the American people, own

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:10.583
all presidential records.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:11.884
The president of the United States.

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:12.285
The minute

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.587
he and someday she leaves office,

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:16.789
they must turn over to you.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.324
All presidential records,

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:20.326
except for a very narrow band of things.

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:21.261
That are considered private,

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:22.495
including a diary.

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:25.164
There is nothing from the FBI materials

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:25.765
that have been released,

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:26.899
nothing that the president

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.002
with the president kept in Mar-A-Lago

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:32.138
that that is within the band of private.

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:34.874
He kept our materials to Natalie.

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.709
Appreciate it so much.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:37.310
Former President

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.545
Trump is expected to be arraigned Tuesday

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.046
in Miami

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:40.813
federal court

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:42.615
following his historic indictment

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.250
for mishandling classified documents.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.051
Now, officials

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:46.886
say law enforcement is scrambling

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.187
to prepare security measures

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:48.655
and the Justice

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:49.956
Department is already moving

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:52.058
additional resources to South Florida.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:53.326
It's notable

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:54.427
that special counsel Jack

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:55.194
Smith obtained

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:56.629
the indictment in Miami

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:58.431
and not in Washington, D.C.,

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:58.698
to help

00:04:58.698 --> 00:04:59.766
protect the case

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:00.967
from potential backlash

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:03.069
over the location of the trial.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:03.469
CNN's

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:05.438
Kaitlin Poulets is live for us outside

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:06.773
the courthouse in Miami.

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:07.407
And Caitlin,

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:08.241
I guess the first question is,

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:09.976
what can we expect to actually see

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:10.777
on Tuesday?

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:14.647
Well, so

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:15.748
we are going to be

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:18.151
able to see what happens

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:19.686
outside the courthouse.

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:22.388
But as far as pictures, video

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:23.256
of what happens

00:05:23.256 --> 00:05:24.290
inside the courthouse,

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:25.758
that just is not something

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:27.093
that federal court does.

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.861
Federal court does not allow

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:31.197
the sort of images of defendants

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:32.632
inside courtrooms

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:34.100
walking into courtrooms.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.169
Anything inside the courthouse

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:38.271
that you even saw in the New York

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:40.673
State arraignment of Donald Trump,

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:42.041
where there were images of him

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.576
walking down the hall into the courtroom,

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:45.411
and then there were photographs of him

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:46.479
inside the courtroom

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.047
before the proceedings started.

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:51.784
No video, no photos in federal court.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.786
So that is a big difference.

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:56.356
But this is, you know, federal property

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:57.390
all around us.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.659
This is a pretty secure complex.

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.160
And so we do expect to see

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.829
a lot of security here,

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:03.830
a lot of presence

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.431
from the federal government

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:06.199
to make sure

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:06.799
that the former

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:08.267
president of the United States

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.670
is protected as a criminal defendant

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.939
and that these grounds stay secure.

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:14.974
So this is quite a complex.

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:17.043
And this is also Miami federal court.

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:18.644
This is not a federal court

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:20.146
that hasn't seen

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:22.815
a high security defendants before.

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:25.184
Man Manuel Noriega was on trial

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:26.386
here for seven months,

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:27.887
several years ago

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.455
in the federal court in Miami.

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.190
He was held here as well.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:32.392
Panama any dictator.

00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:34.527
So this is a very

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:35.695
this is the sort of thing

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:37.163
that this courthouse

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:38.798
has already been through,

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:40.366
really high security incidents.

00:06:40.366 --> 00:06:41.067
But we're going to have to see

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:42.068
how this plays out.

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:43.302
With Donald Trump himself,

00:06:43.302 --> 00:06:46.239
he is a defendant like no other. The good

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:50.576
just so much going on, so many questions.

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:50.810
Okay.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:51.911
Well, part of the reason

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:53.513
I think we're both want to talk to you

00:06:53.513 --> 00:06:54.714
is because you've covered this

00:06:54.714 --> 00:06:55.648
so closely,

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:56.449
so in depth,

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:57.016
so in the weeds

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:58.317
over the course of the better

00:06:58.317 --> 00:07:00.052
part of the last year, to some degree,

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:00.887
there's one element

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:01.154
that I think

00:07:01.154 --> 00:07:01.821
we've heard more

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:02.622
from President

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:03.356
Trump's team

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:05.024
over the course of the last day or two

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:06.692
that they seem to be focusing on.

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:07.326
Trump attorney

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:08.060
Jim Trusty

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.162
accused the top DOJ

00:07:09.162 --> 00:07:11.364
national security lawyer of misconduct

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:11.998
in the process

00:07:11.998 --> 00:07:13.266
of forming this indictment.

00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:15.201
Help us understand the context

00:07:15.201 --> 00:07:17.270
and potential validity of those claims.

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:20.273
Right.

00:07:20.273 --> 00:07:21.073
Well, we're still trying

00:07:21.073 --> 00:07:22.675
to gather more information on this

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:23.543
because it appears

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:25.812
that there is some communication

00:07:25.812 --> 00:07:27.213
to a judge in D.C.

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:29.482
that is under seal. So still secret.

00:07:29.916 --> 00:07:31.818
So we can't get a full understanding

00:07:31.818 --> 00:07:33.052
of that at this time.

00:07:33.052 --> 00:07:34.153
But what Jim

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:35.421
Trustee did say on

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:36.522
CNN last night

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.691
is that they are very unhappy

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:40.193
with a prosecutor

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:42.195
on this special counsel's office team,

00:07:42.195 --> 00:07:43.362
that they believe

00:07:43.362 --> 00:07:44.630
that he may have been trying

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:45.798
to pressure

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:46.632
a lawyer

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:48.734
to a number of witnesses

00:07:48.935 --> 00:07:50.970
in this investigation.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:53.239
And so that is something

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:54.974
that we should be watching.

00:07:54.974 --> 00:07:56.642
But in this situation,

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:58.611
and also with the indictment itself,

00:07:58.611 --> 00:08:00.446
there is a lot of material

00:08:00.446 --> 00:08:02.114
in the court system

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:04.183
that is being looked at by judges,

00:08:04.183 --> 00:08:06.185
including the indictment

00:08:06.185 --> 00:08:08.421
that we just have not seen. Right.

00:08:08.421 --> 00:08:11.090
It is all confidential at this time.

00:08:11.557 --> 00:08:13.826
And so there is this effort

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:15.761
now to understand, you know,

00:08:15.761 --> 00:08:17.430
what is actually on paper versus

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.131
what people are saying publicly

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:20.700
about what's happening behind the scenes

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:21.501
in the federal court.

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:23.269
And as this happens

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:25.705
and as this indictment is brought,

00:08:26.005 --> 00:08:27.240
Jax Smith,

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.508
the special counsel,

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:30.877
